  // never resolved on its own ("Failed to guess stack use for 16").
  "(method 62 rigid-body-object)": [[16, "vector"]],
  // (method 83 rigid-body-object): sp+16 is a 136-byte scratch region: a
  // rigid-body-impact gets built in its first 68 bytes (passed to (method 84
  // rigid-body-object) and read as plain vectors at +0/+32 for a
  // rigid-body-control-method-24 add-force! call, matching rigid-body-impact's
  // own point/velocity fields), then the function keeps writing past that
  // (a cached process-focusable-method-57 float at +112, working vectors at
  // +80/+96) for its own impulse math. Declaring the region as
  // "rigid-body-impact" (its own 0x44 size) left every access past offset 68
